Here's a few hairbrained ideas offered for maybe NetHack 3.1 if it's in
the offing:

NEW CHARACTERS:

1) Archer: he would be supreme with bows and crossbows, of course, very
high dex, he'd practically never miss. Could be pretty avergae otherwise
except that he'd be second only to the rogue in picking locks and
whatnot (all that hand-eye coordination at work). To make the character
worth having might mean adding some spice and variety to the bowed
weaponry, i.e., add some special arrows and crossbow bolts which do
various types of extra damage (fire, cold, poison, shock, sleep, etc.).
There could also be certain special throwing projectiles like the
shurikens (which our bow would be _very_ good with, natch): hand
grenades, stinkbombs which fill a room with sleep-gas, etc.
2) Alchemist: he would be the master of potions and gems (alchemists
were always mucking around with metals, trying to make gold and so
forth). Would always automatically know what any potion or gem is, and
would introduce a couple of new tricks to the game: combining potions to
create new ones, and dropping gems into potions to alter them. These
would not involve any new commands: you'd #d(ip) one potion into
another, or d(rop) a gem into a potion which you've placed on the
ground. Now, anybody could do these things, but only the alchemist
always know what each gem and potion is (without having to read an
identify scroll or whatever), and so would always know what to combine
with what to get what. This would add new interest and relevance to
gems. Of course, combining cursed items would have, ah,
explosive results. Like quaffing a potion, the results of altering one
would sometimes be obvious, sometimes not, if you weren't an alchemist.
Alchemists would also be pretty good with other magic, though not as
good as wizards or priests, of course.
3) Lion tamer: hsi (or her) special ability is obvious, I think - taming
pets. Would start out with a bigger tougher pet than others - say a wolf
or jaguar instead of the little dog or kitten. And, more classes of
beasties would be domesticatable by this character than by the others.
I'm thinking basically of all the non-sentient mammals, so that would
includes apes, canines, felines, bats, unicorns of like alignment,
bugbears, lemures, leocrottas, owlbears, rats, and ?

NEW ROOM:

Opium den: full of @'s, also full of gems, rings, and amulets. Catch is
that you are hallucinating the moment you walk in. So, you don't know
exactly what's attacking you, meaning whatever special attacks they have
will catch you by surprise, and at least you'll die with a silly smile
on your face, eh?

Just a few cents' worth....

